.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt CUDA-NATIVE-INFO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cuda-native-info
.Nd show native CUDA Driver API devices and versions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json | Fl -jsonl | Fl -schema
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility initializes
.Xr libcuda 3
and prints its driver version, native library version, and visible devices.
Text is the default output.
Device memory is reported in bytes.
The attribute names are stable JSON keys and are also used in the text view.
No Linux compatibility layer is used.
.Pp
The default nvrm provider is a stub in this release and reports an error.
Select the fake provider for a deterministic, hardware-free report.
Fake device properties are synthetic test values.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl -schema"
.It Fl -json
Write one JSON document on one line.
The document contains a device array and its count.
.It Fl -jsonl
Write JSON Lines: one header, one device record per visible device in
enumeration order, and one end record containing the device count.
.It Fl -schema
Write the JSON Schema shared by both JSON modes without initializing the
provider.
The schema identifier in each output record is
.Dq cuda-native-info/1 .
.It Fl -help
Print usage and exit successfully.
.El
.Pp
The output-mode options exclude each other.
Positional arguments and unknown options are usage errors.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ".Ev CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES"
.It Ev CUDA_NATIVE_BACKEND
Select
.Dq fake
or
.Dq nvrm .
The default is
.Dq nvrm .
.It Ev CUDA_NATIVE_FAKE_PROFILE
Select the fake profile list; the default is
.Dq gb206 .
Use
.Dq gb206,gb10
for two devices.
.It Ev CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
Filter and reorder devices by physical index or GPU UUID.
See
.Xr libcuda 3
for the exact rules.
.El
.Sh OUTPUT SCHEMA
The JSON document and JSON Lines header contain
.Dv cuda_version
and
.Dv cuda_native_version
objects.
Each version has its canonical
.Dv string
and integer
.Dv major ,
.Dv minor ,
and
.Dv patch
parts, so consumers do not need to parse the string for comparisons.
Device records contain the ordinal, name, GPU UUID, total memory in bytes, and
the attribute object.
A query failure produces a JSON error record in either JSON mode and a diagnostic
on standard error in text mode.
The committed schema is installed as
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/cuda-native-info-1.schema.json .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A successful empty device list is not an error.
Exit status 1 indicates a provider, query, or output failure; status 2 indicates
a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print two synthetic devices as text:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
env CUDA_NATIVE_BACKEND=fake CUDA_NATIVE_FAKE_PROFILE=gb206,gb10 cuda-native-info
.Ed
.Pp
From a source checkout, validate a JSON Lines stream using the project's
supported-keyword validator:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
env CUDA_NATIVE_BACKEND=fake cuda-native-info --jsonl |
    python3 tests/libnvrm/schema_validate.py \
    lib/libcuda/schema/cuda-native-info-1.schema.json
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libcuda 3
.Sh HISTORY
The utility first appeared in cuda-native 0.1.0.
